# Unstable Glyphbridge ({3}{W}{W}, Craft with artifact {3}{W}{W}) and Sandswirl Wanderglyph, a 5/3 flier: "Whenever an opponent casts a spell during
# their turn, they can't attack you or planeswalkers you control this turn. Each opponent who attacked you or a planeswalker you control this turn can't
# cast spells." Turn one: five mana with a single white source is refused (one {W} short, CR 601.2f), then Black Lotus makes the cast possible and is
# sacrificed. Turn three: the same five mana is refused for the craft, then a Plains pays it, and the Black Lotus in the graveyard is the material.
# Turn four: Bot2's Lightning Bolt (cast when nothing is barred) lays the rule on its Savannah Lions, which then cannot attack Bot1: it carries the rule
# and Bot1 is untouched by any attack. Turn six: nothing was cast, so the Lions attack (the bar ended with turn four), and having attacked Bot1, Bot2
# cannot cast its second Lightning Bolt (a spell it could otherwise cast: the Mox Ruby is untapped and pays).

